# OctoAcme Project Management Knowledge Base Summary

This document is a quick team-facing summary of the repository and its intended use.

## Overview
This knowledge base captures the team’s operating model for cross-functional project delivery. It is intentionally practical, lightweight, and designed to improve clarity without adding bureaucracy.

## Lifecycle
- Initiation: align on problem, stakeholders, and early success metrics.
- Planning: define scope, milestones, backlog, and responsibilities.
- Execution: build with rhythm, quality checks, and visible blockers.
- Release: validate readiness and communicate clearly.
- Retrospective: capture learning and convert it to action.

## Roles
- Product lead defines outcomes and priorities.
- Project manager coordinates planning, execution, and communication.
- Engineers deliver and validate implementation.
- Stakeholders provide decisions, inputs, and approvals.

## Standard tools
- One-pager / project charter
- Risk register
- Backlog with acceptance criteria
- Weekly status communication
- Retrospective action items

## Recommended practices
- Keep artifacts visible in the project repo.
- Review the team’s process docs during planning and retrospectives.
- Update the knowledge base when practices materially change.

